{"name":"Deep Dungeon","hex":"#553d3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"dungeon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An underground prison or vault, typically built underneath a castle.","The low area between two drumlins."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To imprison in a dungeon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dungeon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deep Dungeon","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Dungeon (ディープダンジョン) is a series of role-playing video games developed by HummingBirdSoft. The first two installments were released on the Family Computer Disk System by Square's label Disk Original Group (DOG); the third one was released on the regular Family Computer by Square directly and the final one by Asmik."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Dungeon","wikidata":"Q5250165"},{"title":"Dungeon","blocks":[{"text":"A dungeon is a type of prison, usually an underground room or cell, in which prisoners are held. Dungeons are generally associated with medieval castles. They are closely connected in concept both to the prison and the oubliette, and the words are sometimes used interchangeably. In the popular imagination, a dungeon is claustrophobic, strong, damp, and located in a castle under the direct control of a medieval lord. This intentional unpleasantness and personal control over a dungeon contrasts to the modern prison, which provides a civil function."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/BlarneyCastle5.jpg/330px-BlarneyCastle5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeon","wikidata":"Q89753"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Deep_dungeon_package_edited2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Deep_dungeon_package_edited2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeep_dungeon_package_edited2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/500px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/1280px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/500px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dungeon door in the Zrinski Castle in Čakovec, Croatia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Oubliettes.Bastille.png/330px-Oubliettes.Bastille.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi